Experiential Acoustic Sculpture Garden
709.2 / 720.28 Environmental art; architectural acoustics

NAME: Giardino Sonoro
LOCATION: San Sperate, Sardinia
ARTIST: Pinuccio Sciola
LIFESPAN: 1942–2016
ORIGIN: Family citrus grove converted 1990s
STATUS: Open-air sound museum

MATERIALS:
  PRIMARY: Carved basalt
  SECONDARY: Limestone
  FORM: Tall grooved monoliths

INTERACTION:
  METHOD: Rubbing or striking incised grooves
  OUTPUT: Resonant musical tones
  PRINCIPLE: Precise incision releases latent stone vibration

FUNDAMENTALS:
  - Inert rock treated as latent acoustic instrument
  - Sculpture + landscape + sound as single experiential system
  - Hidden material properties made audible through geometry
  - Self-taught craft applied to site-specific installation

CONTEXT:
  ACCOUNT: @parametricarch
  THEME: Unexpected sensory potential in natural materials
  FIELD: Parametric design / material innovation / architecture
